WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.710
Gold can be found in
the ground as metal.

2
00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:05.490
No reaction is needed to free it.

3
00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:06.950
Iron is different.

4
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.170
Dig for iron and you
find a rock called ore.

5
00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:12.950
Is the iron just mixed
in with the rock?

6
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.270
Gold and iron are both metals.

7
00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:19.310
So why is one found as metal,
and the other locked in rock?

8
00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:22.050
In this mission, you'll
put metals in order,

9
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:24.470
from most to least reactive.

10
00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:27.450
You'll see one metal push
another out of its compound.

11
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:31.830
And you'll see how carbon
gets iron out of its ore.

12
00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.050
Your mission: explain why
gold is found as metal,

13
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.710
but iron is locked in rock.
